===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|gabalō||fork|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|ghabh-||boar-spear, fork, groin|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|gavala|lang=osx}}, {{term|gaflia||fork|lang=osx}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|gabala||twi-pronged or multi-pronged fork|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|gaffel|lang=nl}}, {{term|gavel||fork|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Gabel||fork|lang=de}}, {{etyl|sga|-}} {{term|gabul||fork, forked branch|lang=sga}}. More at {{l|en|gaffle}}.

